the scheduler down.",[150,1431,1432,1435,1436,1439,1440,1443,1444,1447],{},[167,1433,1434],{},"createEventLogger"," formats the stream into single-line ",[167,1437,1438],{},"[sched] …"," entries\n(console by default; point ",[167,1441,1442],{},"write"," at pino for structured output, or use\n",[167,1445,1446],{},"filter"," to keep only the event types you care about):",[218,1449,1454],{"className":1450,"code":1452,"language":1453},[1451],"language-text","[sched] tick: 3 due\n[sched] claim publish-video run=ab12cd34 attempt=1\n[sched] dispatch publish-video run=ab12cd34 runner=http attempt=1\n[sched] retry publish-video run=ab12cd34 attempt=1 backoff=60000ms (next 2026-08-16 12:01:00Z)\n[sched] missed-slot publish-video sched=publish-video scheduled 2026-08-16 03:00:00Z (32400000ms late)\n[sched] reaped 2 zombie lock(s) older than 2026-08-16 11:30:00Z\n","text",[167,1455,1452],{"__ignoreMap":223},[608,1457,1459],{"id":1458},"still-possible-wrapping-the-storage-seam","Still possible: wrapping the Storage seam",[150,1461,1462,1463,1465,1466,1469],{},"The engine's storage calls remain a valid, lower-level observation point —\nevery engine action (due scan, claim, completion, zombie reap) is a ",[167,1464,75],{},"\nmethod call, so a proxy logs the lifecycle at a coarser granularity (e.g. to\ncapture ",[585,1467,1468],{},"skipped"," claims, which the event stream intentionally leaves silent):",[218,1471,1473],{"className":220,"code":1472,"language":222,"meta":223,"style":223},"import type { Storage } from '@schedjs\u002Fcore';\n\nfunction loggingStorage(s: Storage): Storage {\n  return {\n    ...s,\n    async listDueTasks(now) {\n      const due = await s.listDueTasks(now);\n      console.log(`[sched] tick: ${due.length} due`);\n      return due;\n    },\n    async claimTask(name, at) {\n      const ok = await s.claimTask(name, at);\n      console.log(`[sched] claim ${name} → ${ok ? 'taken' : 'skipped (locked\u002Fpaused)'}`);\n      return ok;\n    },\n    async complete